# Line endings are content in this repository.
#
# kranji-gloss-seed is content-addressed: SeedIsImmutableTest hashes the bytes
# of every seeded partition and compares them against a digest committed
# beside the data. Git for Windows ships core.autocrlf=true in its system
# config, so without this file a fresh checkout rewrites every seed file as
# CRLF, the digest stops matching, and the build fails on a machine where
# nothing is wrong with the code. `git status` stays clean the whole time,
# because git converts back on read - which is what makes it expensive to
# find rather than merely annoying.
#
# text=auto lets git normalise to LF on commit; eol=lf makes every checkout
# LF whatever the platform would otherwise do. Nothing tracked here is
# binary, so one rule covers all of it.

* text=auto eol=lf
